---
import DocsLayout from "../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import Code from "../components/Code.astro";
import TokenTable from "../components/api/TokenTable.astro";
import PropertiesTable from "../components/api/PropertiesTable.astro";
import InstanceNote from "../components/api/InstanceNote.astro";
import { defineSections } from "../lib/sections";

const S = defineSections([
  { id: "introduction", label: "Introduction", heading: false },
  { id: "sizes", label: "Sizes", heading: "FAB sizes" },
  { id: "extended", label: "Extended", heading: "Extended FAB" },
  { id: "fab-menu", label: "FAB menu" },
  { id: "migration", label: "Migration" },
  { id: "initialization", label: "Initialization" },
  { id: "methods", label: "Methods" },
  { id: "properties", label: "Properties" },
]);
---
<DocsLayout page="floating_action_button">
<div class="container">
  <div class="row">
    <div class="s12 m8 offset-m1 xl7 offset-xl1">

  <Section {...S.introduction}>
    <p class="flow-text">Use one FAB for the primary action, or a FAB menu for related labelled actions. The menu opens on click and keeps ordinary Tab navigation.</p>
    <p>See <a href="#fab-menu">FAB menu</a> for markup and <a href="#migration">migration guidance</a> for removed FAB variants and speed dials.</p>
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.sizes}>
        <p>
          A FAB is <code>circle extra</code> (or its alias
          <code>circle large</code>): 56dp, 16dp corners,
          <code>primary-container</code>, elevation 3. The medium and large size classes
          go alongside the <code>extra</code>. The corner grows with the
          container, so a bigger FAB is not simply a scaled-up one.
        </p>
        <div class="fab-size-demo">
          <div>
            <button type="button" class="circle extra" aria-label="Add"><span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">add</span></button>
            <span class="body-small">default<br>56dp</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <button type="button" class="circle extra medium" aria-label="Add"><span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">add</span></button>
            <span class="body-small"><code>medium</code><br>80dp</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <button type="button" class="circle extra large" aria-label="Add"><span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">add</span></button>
            <span class="body-small"><code>large</code><br>96dp</span>
          </div>
        </div>
<Code code={`
<button type="button" class="circle extra" aria-label="Add">
  <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">add</span>
</button>
<button type="button" class="circle extra medium" aria-label="Add">
  <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">add</span>
</button>
<button type="button" class="circle extra large" aria-label="Add">
  <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">add</span>
</button>
`} />
        <div class="docs-table-scroll">
        <table class="striped">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Size</th>
                    <th>Class</th>
                    <th>Container</th>
                    <th>Corner</th>
                    <th>Icon</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td>Default</td><td><code>circle extra</code></td><td>56dp</td><td>16dp</td><td>24dp</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Medium</td><td><code>circle extra medium</code></td><td>80dp</td><td>20dp</td><td>26dp</td></tr>
                <tr><td>Large</td><td><code>circle extra large</code></td><td>96dp</td><td>28dp</td><td>36dp</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
        </div>
        <p>
          The large size needs the <code>extra</code>:
          <code>circle large</code> on its own is the alias for the default
          56dp FAB, and keeps that meaning.
        </p>
        <p>
          On an <code>&lt;a&gt;</code>, add <code>button</code> — the size
          classes only match <code>button</code> or <code>a.button</code>.
        </p>
<Code code={`
<a class="button circle extra medium" href="#!" aria-label="Add">
  <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">add</span>
</a>
`} />
        <p>
          Each size is the same four custom properties, so a one-off size is
          a matter of resetting them rather than writing new rules.
        </p>
        <div class="docs-table-scroll">
        <TokenTable>
            <tr><td><code>--md-comp-fab-container-height</code></td><td>56px</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>--md-comp-fab-container-width</code></td><td>56px</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>--md-comp-fab-container-shape</code></td><td>16px</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>--md-comp-fab-icon-size</code></td><td>24px</td></tr>
        </TokenTable>
        </div>
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.extended}>
        <p>
          <code>extend small</code> is the extended FAB: an icon plus a label at
          56dp, 16dp corners, 8dp between the two. Wrap the label in its own
          <code>&lt;span&gt;</code> — the order of the two spans is the
          placement, and the wrapper is what earns the 16dp leading inset.
        </p>
        <div class="fab-size-demo">
          <div>
            <button type="button" class="extend small"><span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">add</span><span>Create</span></button>
            <span class="body-small"><code>extend small</code><br>56dp</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <button type="button" class="extend medium"><span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">add</span><span>Create</span></button>
            <span class="body-small"><code>extend medium</code><br>80dp</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <button type="button" class="extend large"><span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">add</span><span>Create</span></button>
            <span class="body-small"><code>extend large</code><br>96dp</span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <button type="button" class="extend small"><span>Create</span><span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">add</span></button>
            <span class="body-small"><code>extend small</code><br>trailing icon</span>
          </div>
        </div>
<Code code={`
<button type="button" class="extend small">
  <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">add</span><span>Create</span>
</button>
<button type="button" class="extend medium">
  <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">add</span><span>Create</span>
</button>
`} />
        <p>
          The size axis is <code>small</code>, <code>medium</code> and
          <code>large</code>, and the label role grows with the container:
          <code>title-medium</code>, <code>title-large</code>,
          <code>headline-small</code>. <code>extend small</code> is 56dp on a
          symmetric 16dp inset. Always specify a size; the sizeless baseline extended FAB has been removed.
        </p>
        <p>
          The container colour is a role rather than a value.
          <code>primary-container</code> is the default;
          <code>secondary-container</code> and <code>tertiary-container</code>
          are the other two. Each sets the container and the label colour
          together, so the hover and focus state layers follow the role with
          it.
        </p>
        <div class="fab-size-demo">
          <div>
            <button type="button" class="extend small"><span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">edit</span><span>Compose</span></button>
            <span class="body-small">default<br><code>primary-container</code></span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <button type="button" class="extend small secondary-container"><span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">edit</span><span>Compose</span></button>
            <span class="body-small"><code>secondary-container</code></span>
          </div>
          <div>
            <button type="button" class="extend small tertiary-container"><span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">edit</span><span>Compose</span></button>
            <span class="body-small"><code>tertiary-container</code></span>
          </div>
        </div>
<Code code={`
<button type="button" class="extend small secondary-container">
  <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">edit</span><span>Compose</span>
</button>
`} />
        <div class="docs-table-scroll">
        <TokenTable>
            <tr><td><code>--md-comp-extended-fab-container-height</code></td><td>56px (80px <code>medium</code>, 96px <code>large</code>)</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>--md-comp-extended-fab-container-shape</code></td><td>16px (20px <code>medium</code>, 28px <code>large</code>)</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>--md-comp-extended-fab-icon-size</code></td><td>24px (28px <code>medium</code>, 36px <code>large</code>)</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>--md-comp-extended-fab-leading-space</code></td><td>16px (26px <code>medium</code>, 28px <code>large</code>)</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>--md-comp-extended-fab-icon-label-space</code></td><td>8px (12px <code>medium</code>, 16px <code>large</code>)</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>--md-comp-extended-fab-trailing-space</code></td><td>16px (26px <code>medium</code>, 28px <code>large</code>)</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>--md-comp-extended-fab-container-color</code></td><td><code>--md-sys-color-primary-container</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>--md-comp-extended-fab-label-text-color</code></td><td><code>--md-sys-color-on-primary-container</code></td></tr>
        </TokenTable>
        </div>
  </Section>
  <Section {...S["fab-menu"]}>
        <p>
          <code>fab-menu</code> is the FAB that expands into a list of
          labelled actions. The trigger is an ordinary FAB; the actions are a
          <code>&lt;ul&gt;</code> (or <code>&lt;menu&gt;</code>) of pills, each
          an icon and a label at 56dp on a full corner. Click the FAB to
          expand; click it again, click outside, or press
          <kbd>Esc</kbd> to collapse.
        </p>
        <p>
          Expanded is the framework's, not yours: the constructor stamps
          <code>aria-expanded</code> on the trigger and
          <code>open()</code> / <code>close()</code> move it along with the
          <code>active</code> class. Do not write either into the markup.
        </p>
        <div class="fab-menu-demo">
          <div class="fab-menu" id="fab-menu-primary">
            <button type="button" class="button extra circle" aria-label="Create">
              <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">add</span>
              <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">close</span>
            </button>
            <ul>
              <li><button type="button"><span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">mode_edit</span><span>Compose</span></button></li>
              <li><button type="button"><span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">image</span><span>Add photo</span></button></li>
              <li><button type="button"><span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">mic</span><span>Record</span></button></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="fab-menu secondary-container" id="fab-menu-secondary">
            <button type="button" class="button extra circle" aria-label="Create, secondary">
              <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">add</span>
              <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">close</span>
            </button>
            <ul>
              <li><button type="button"><span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">mode_edit</span><span>Compose</span></button></li>
              <li><button type="button"><span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">image</span><span>Add photo</span></button></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="fab-menu tertiary-container" id="fab-menu-tertiary">
            <button type="button" class="button extra circle" aria-label="Create, tertiary">
              <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">add</span>
              <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">close</span>
            </button>
            <ul>
              <li><button type="button"><span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">mode_edit</span><span>Compose</span></button></li>
              <li><button type="button"><span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">image</span><span>Add photo</span></button></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
<Code code={`
<div class="fab-menu">
  <button type="button" class="button extra circle" aria-label="Create">
    <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">add</span>
    <span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">close</span>
  </button>
  <ul>
    <li><button type="button"><span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">mode_edit</span><span>Compose</span></button></li>
    <li><button type="button"><span class="material-symbols" aria-hidden="true">image</span><span>Add photo</span></button></li>
  </ul>
</div>
`} />
        <p>
          Expanded, the FAB is the close button: the same disc on a full
          corner, the solid role colour rather than its container, and a 20dp
          glyph. Give the trigger a second icon and it becomes the close
          glyph — the first shows while collapsed, the second while expanded,
          and only ever one of them is in the box. With one icon the morph is
          the whole affordance.
        </p>
        <p>
          The colour axis is the same three roles as the extended FAB, and one
          class moves both halves: the actions take
          <code>primary-container</code> (the default),
          <code>secondary-container</code> or
          <code>tertiary-container</code>, and the close button takes the
          matching solid <code>primary</code>, <code>secondary</code> or
          <code>tertiary</code>. Material 3 pairs them that way deliberately —
          the close button is the louder of the two.
        </p>
<Code code={`
<div class="fab-menu secondary-container">…</div>
`} />
        <p>
          <code>FloatingActionButton</code> owns the menu state. It opens upward on click, closes on Escape, outside click or action activation, and returns focus when closing would hide the focused action. Closed actions are inert. Ordinary Tab navigation is preserved.        </p>
        <p>
          Beyond six actions the stagger runs out and the rest arrive
          together, which is past where Material 3 stops recommending them.
        </p>
        <div class="docs-table-scroll">
        <TokenTable>
            <tr><td><code>--md-comp-fab-menu-close-button-container-height</code></td><td>56px</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>--md-comp-fab-menu-close-button-container-width</code></td><td>56px</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>--md-comp-fab-menu-close-button-icon-size</code></td><td>20px</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>--md-comp-fab-menu-close-button-between-space</code></td><td>8px</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>--md-comp-fab-menu-close-button-container-color</code></td><td><code>--md-sys-color-primary</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>--md-comp-fab-menu-close-button-icon-color</code></td><td><code>--md-sys-color-on-primary</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>--md-comp-fab-menu-menu-item-container-height</code></td><td>56px</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>--md-comp-fab-menu-menu-item-between-space</code></td><td>4px</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>--md-comp-fab-menu-menu-item-icon-size</code></td><td>24px</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>--md-comp-fab-menu-menu-item-icon-label-space</code></td><td>8px</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>--md-comp-fab-menu-menu-item-leading-space</code></td><td>24px</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>--md-comp-fab-menu-menu-item-trailing-space</code></td><td>24px</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>--md-comp-fab-menu-menu-item-container-color</code></td><td><code>--md-sys-color-primary-container</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>--md-comp-fab-menu-menu-item-label-text-color</code></td><td><code>--md-sys-color-on-primary-container</code></td></tr>
        </TokenTable>
        </div>
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.migration}>
    <p>Replace <code>.fab</code> and <code>.fixed-action-btn</code> speed-dial wrappers with <code>.fab-menu</code> and visible labels on each action. This requires updating the markup, not just renaming the wrapper.</p>
    <p>Remove <code>direction</code>, <code>hoverEnabled</code>, <code>toolbarEnabled</code>, their markup switches and speed-dial-only token overrides. Hover opening and FAB-to-toolbar expansion have been removed. Use the <a href="/toolbars.html">toolbar component</a> for persistent commands.</p>
    <p>Replace <code>circle extra small</code> with <code>circle extra</code> for the current 56dp FAB. Replace sizeless <code>extend</code> with <code>extend small</code>, or choose <code>medium</code> or <code>large</code>. The small extended FAB remains supported. Replace surface color classes on FABs with <code>primary-container</code>, <code>secondary-container</code> or <code>tertiary-container</code> and the matching <code>on-*-container-text</code> for icon-only FABs. General surface utilities remain available for other components.</p>
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.initialization}>
    <p><code>Expressive.AutoInit()</code> initializes <code>.fab-menu</code>. For manual ownership, add <code>no-autoinit</code> and initialize it yourself. There are no component-specific options.</p>
    <Code code={`const instance = Expressive.FloatingActionButton.init(document.querySelector(".fab-menu.no-autoinit"));`} />
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.methods}>
        <InstanceNote plugin="FloatingActionButton" />

        <h5 class="light">.open();</h5>
        <p>Opens the FAB menu.</p>
<Code code={`
instance.open();
`} />

        <h5 class="light">.close();</h5>
        <p>Closes the FAB menu.</p>
<Code code={`
instance.close();
`} />

        <h5 class="light">.destroy();</h5>
        <p>Destroy the plugin instance and tear down its event handlers.</p>
<Code code={`
instance.destroy();
`} />
  </Section>
  <Section {...S.properties}>
        <PropertiesTable el="The DOM element the plugin was initialized with.">
            <tr>
              <td><code>isOpen</code></td>
              <td>Boolean</td>
              <td>Describes the open/close state of the FAB.</td>
            </tr>
  </PropertiesTable>
  </Section>
    </div>

    <div class="hide-on-small-only m3 xl3">
      <div class="toc-wrapper mt-5">
        <nav aria-label="On this page">
          <ul class="section table-of-contents">
            {Object.values(S).map((s) => (
            <li><a href={`#${s.id}`}>{s.label}</a></li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
</DocsLayout>
